      "writtenOn": "2023-01-17T18:50:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e regarding ectool.cc, it\u0027s already taken care for cmd_pwm_get_fan_rpm\n\nYou need to deal with combinations of (ectool, fw) \u003d\u003d (old, new), (new, old).\n\nIf ectool is older, it won\u0027t print \u0027stalled\u0027 properly. So, this will have some affect for those using the tool for testing. This is usually ok because their common practice is to update the OS on test failure.\n\nFor devices which run old FW, we probably need to make ectool continue to print \u0027stalled\u0027 for 0xfffe (and x0000 as well). We can also print \u0027deprecated\u0027 as a warning.",
      "parentUuid": "415e0ae6_ec9c06d9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 255,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 255,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "59842b5b57d110f75b86865b1a2973bd1a698257",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c1257c88_20932d3a",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 255,
      "author": {
        "id": 1365385
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T18:47:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Dai,\nAgree that for devices running with older ectool, it wont print.\nBut, the command(cmd_pwm_get_fan_rpm)  which uses this print doesnt depend on ec host command  to read rpm, but is reading rpm from memory location and printing it.So, i don\u0027t think, we have a way to verify the command version and then to decide about the stall print. In a way,rpm \u003d 0 gives same hint to user, eventhough  the stall print gets missed in boards with old fw.  Also,the moment when rpm is set to 0 in pwm_fan_second(), stall print will appear in ec log. So, it doesnt really impact boards with older fw.",
      "parentUuid": "22a4bbad_59c72e36",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 255,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 255,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "59842b5b57d110f75b86865b1a2973bd1a698257",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8a5fb102_f637a440",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 255,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T19:00:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e In a way, rpm \u003d 0 gives same hint to user, ...\n\nMaybe we should get rid of \u0027case EC_FAN_SPEED_STALLED\u0027 from print_fan, then. Maybe we should get rid of EC_FAN_SPEED_STALLED entirely. To anybody, rpm\u003d0 naturally means the fan is stalled.\n\nNew question: how do you distinguish RPM never measured (\u003d0) v.s. RPM measure to 0?",
      "parentUuid": "c1257c88_20932d3a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 255,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 255,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "59842b5b57d110f75b86865b1a2973bd1a698257",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
