      "writtenOn": "2023-01-23T17:57:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dependency on where rpm value is compared to EC_FAN_SPEED_STALLED is seen only as part of printing info in command response only.\n util/ectool.cc:3650:    case EC_FAN_SPEED_STALLED:\n So, mean to say, donot see any code reference on where any distinction/action on when  rpm is set to zero by itself or due to stalling.\n I think the print reference  is kind of redundant. But, setting rpm to zero , when fan is found to be stalled due to  any reason(no duty cycle/pwm not enable/tacho underflow) makes sense too, as otherwise, rpm value might continue with some prev value otherwsise, if fan gets stalled due to some reason.",
      "parentUuid": "47361432_61c41c2a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 255,
        "startChar": 31,
